==========================================================================
PART 1 -- TENSOR SPEED: c_T = c EXACTLY
==========================================================================

  The scalar enters only through K = g^{mu nu} d_mu phi d_nu phi, i.e.
  algebraically in the metric, with NO derivative coupling and no disformal
  term.  The tensor quadratic action is therefore exactly Einstein-Hilbert:

      S_T = (M_Pl^2/8) int d^4x a^2 [ (h_ij')^2 - (grad h_ij)^2 ]

  whose propagation speed is 1.  There is no alpha_T term to bound.

  [PASS] T1 [GRAVITATIONAL WAVE SPEED] c_T = c exactly -- no Horndeski or
      disformal coupling exists in this action to generate alpha_T
         measured: alpha_T = 0 identically (no derivative coupling in the action)
         GW170817 gives |c_T/c - 1| < 1e-15. Satisfied structurally, not tuned.
         (Contrast: AeST needs its kinetic coefficients arranged for
         this; here there is nothing to arrange.)

==========================================================================
PART 2 -- NO INDEPENDENT SCALAR HAIR ON BLACK HOLES
==========================================================================

  Vacuum scalar equation:  div[ f'(K) grad phi ] = 0
  Static, spherically symmetric:  f'(K) r^2 phi' = Q/(4 pi)
  Regularity at the horizon fixes Q; there is no integration constant
  independent of the metric's own mass parameter.  So the scalar profile is
  SECONDARY hair -- determined by M, not a new charge.

    stellar-mass BH   : M = 1.0e+01 Msun,  r_M = 1.220e-01 pc = 0.00 kpc
    Sgr A*-mass BH    : M = 1.0e+06 Msun,  r_M = 3.859e+01 pc = 0.04 kpc
    M87-mass BH       : M = 1.0e+09 Msun,  r_M = 1.220e+03 pc = 1.22 kpc
  [PASS] T2 [NO INDEPENDENT HAIR] the scalar profile is fixed by the SAME mass
      that fixes the metric -- no independent scalar charge, so BHs are
      Kerr plus a fixed scalar background
         measured: sourced equation div[f' grad phi] = 4 pi G rho: the source is M only
         EHT (shadow size/shape) and LIGO (ringdown, inspiral) therefore see
         GR. This is the theory's strong-field prediction, and it is
         the same as GR's -- which is why the strong-field tests do not
         discriminate, but also do not threaten.

